ys approximately 1K people. Revenue per employee of $1.1M ranks in the above the sector median among Financial Services peers. Stock-based compensation of $23K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 3\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (2/10).","financial_summary":["SLM Corporation is a mid-cap financial services business with a $3.2B market cap on $2.0B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +3% over the past three years and +8% annually across the full decade, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at 19% against a 11% cost of capital, a 8-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 1.6\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and thin 0.9\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 14.7% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and within its sector the business captures 1.9\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.5) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Elevated short interest (10.2% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Fintech disintermediation \u2014 neobanks, embedded finance, and blockchain rails are unbundling the fee streams that traditional banks took for granted.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 21% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Trading at a 58% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"SLM (SLM), Why SLM Is Back In The Spotlight","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/diversified-financials/nasdaq-slm/slm/news/slm-slm-why-slm-is-back-in-the-spotlight","date":"2026-11-10","timestamp":1794302696.306,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.943,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"(SLM) Volatility Zones as Tactical Triggers","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/24/SLM_Volatility_Zones_as_Tactical_Triggers_110926123801_1794245881.html","date":"2026-11-09","timestamp":1794245881.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"SLM Cuts 2026 EPS Outlook, Raises Charge-Off Forecast: What's Ahead?","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3020792/slm-cuts-2026-eps-outlook-raises-charge-off-forecast-what-s-ahead?cid=CS-ZC-FT-analyst_blog%7Ccompany_news_finance_sector-3020792","date":"2026-11-02","timestamp":1793633460.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.29